    "head_commit_message": "refactor(sim): the lane and its fights in the crate (spec 39 step 9b-i)\n\nLaneSimulation, CombatResolver and PlayerRoster port to the crate as they\nwere (native/rust/src/lane.rs): resolve is the fight, Lane the nodes'\nowners and garrisons, the waves and moving blockers by id, and each side's\nunits harvesting. A tick is march, then each listed wave's arrival.\n\nThe binding LaneState (lane/binding.rs) emits each wave's events on\nSimEvents before the next arrives, holding base_mut so main.gd's handlers\ncall back into the lane between arrivals where they did: a mover spawned by\na capture's suspicion meets a later wave that tick, and a wave harvested\nmid-tick still arrives. A moving blocker's dictionary stays its truth, as\nGDScript shared it. main.gd's roster and farm loop become harvest and\nunits_of; the lane's view, TaskForceDispatch and their tests read\nLaneState. The three GDScript classes and their gdUnit tests are gone.\n\nOutcomes unchanged: the same fights, captures and events in the same\norder; no digest battle has a lane. Step 9b split into 9b-i to 9b-iii under\nthe user's standing leave.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011AyPi2FjB2k5bSUCtZ1pk4",
